<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; Prayer in the Christian Life" cic="CCC 2558-2589" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What is prayer according to the Catechism and according to Saint Thérèse of Lisieux?</li>
<li>Who takes the initiative in prayer: us or God? Why?</li>
<li>Name three fundamental attitudes for Christian prayer.</li>
<li>What are the three main expressions of prayer?</li>
<li>What lesson does the parable of the tax collector and the Pharisee teach us about prayer?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. Describe your current prayer routine. How often do you pray? How do you feel when you do?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Be honest. If you do not have a routine, say so. The important thing is to start from where you are.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Have you ever had an experience where you felt that God was listening to you in a special way? What was it like?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">If it has never happened, do not worry. Prayer does not depend on feelings.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. What type of prayer comes most naturally to you: spoken words, meditation, or silent contemplation?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Each of us has a &laquo;door&raquo; through which it is easier to enter into prayer. What is yours?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. Is there anything in your life that prevents you from praying more often? (laziness, distractions, lack of time, doubts...)</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Identifying the obstacles is the first step to overcoming them.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. If you knew that God always listens to you and loves you, what would you say to him today if you could speak face to face?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Write the first thing that comes to mind. Do not overthink it.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Pray the Our Father as if for the first time</h4>
<p>Take five minutes. Say each phrase slowly, pausing briefly after each one. If a word catches your attention, stay there for a moment. When you finish, write which phrase impacted you most and why.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Meditate with a psalm</h4>
<p>Choose one of these psalms: Ps 23 (The Lord is my shepherd), Ps 27 (The Lord is my light), Ps 63 (My soul thirsts for you). Read it slowly three times. The first time, just listen. The second, underline the words that speak to you. The third, sit in silence with one phrase. Write what you discovered.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Keep a prayer journal for one week</h4>
<p>Each day, write: what you said to God, how you felt, what Scripture passage accompanied you, and how the rest of the day went. At the end of the week, read back over what you wrote. Do you see any pattern?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;Pray without ceasing.&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; 1 Thessalonians 5:17</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord, teach me to pray.<br />
I do not know what to say, I do not know where to begin.<br />
Sometimes I get distracted, sometimes I get bored,<br />
sometimes I feel like I am talking to myself.<br />
But you sought me first.<br />
You thirst for me before I thirst for you.<br />
Take my poor prayer and turn it into a dialogue of love.<br />
May my restless heart find rest in you.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

